---
description: Apply when CI fails, a build is red, or a test is flaky
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

- Read the FIRST failure in the run (later ones are cascade) and the actual failing output — quote the decisive line. List what changed: the diff, plus what CI re-resolves every run (dependencies, images, runners).
- One diagnostic rerun maximum (same commit, only if unsure): same failure → deterministic; gone → flake or infra. Rerun-until-green as a fix is forbidden.
- Classify, then act: code bug (deterministic, from the diff → debug protocol) · broken test (prove the code right before fixing the expectation) · flake (same commit passes and fails → quarantine) · infra (runner/disk/registry — rerun legitimate for this class only) · drift (dependency resolved new → pin now, upgrade deliberately).
- Reproduce locally with the command CI ran (from the workflow file, not memory). Local-passes-CI-fails → diff the environments (versions, env vars, parallelism, timezone, test order).
- Flakes are real bugs (shared state, ordering, time, unawaited async, ports): fix the root cause if affordable now, else quarantine WITH a ticket linked in the skip marker — a skip without a ticket is a deletion. Never sleeps or wider timeouts as the fix.
- Main red: fix forward only if minutes away, else revert first. Entangled commits → `git bisect` with the CI command. Never debug by pushing guess-commits — every push costs the whole queue.
